## ⚡ n8n Multi-Setup – Version 2.6.3 Update (Python + Node 20 + Playwright)

This update documents the current production stack based on n8n 2.6.3, Node.js 20 and Python 3.9, plus Playwright browser automation support.

### Key versions

* **n8n:** 2.6.3
* **Node.js:** 20.x
* **Python:** 3.9 + virtualenv
* **Custom image:** `n8n-custom:2.6.3`
* **Playwright:** `1.48.0`
* **Browser:** Chromium (Playwright-managed)

### Python packages

The custom image includes the existing Python automation/data libraries plus:

```text
playwright==1.48.0
```

### Playwright / Chromium

Playwright requires both the Python package and a browser runtime. The production container was enabled in-place to avoid downtime, and Chromium was verified successfully.

Future image builds should include:

```Dockerfile
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir \
    requests \
    urllib3 \
    httpx \
    pandas \
    numpy \
    scipy \
    pydantic \
    python-dateutil \
    pytz \
    python-dotenv \
    tenacity \
    rich \
    loguru \
    jsonschema \
    lxml \
    beautifulsoup4 \
    xmltodict \
    openpyxl \
    xlrd \
    sqlalchemy \
    psycopg2-binary \
    redis \
    boto3 \
    cryptography \
    pyjwt \
    playwright==1.48.0

RUN python -m playwright install-deps chromium

RUN mkdir -p /home/node/.cache/ms-playwright \
    && chown -R node:node /home/node/.cache

USER node
RUN python -m playwright install chromium
USER root
```

### Runtime verification

Check Playwright:

```bash
docker exec n8n-multi-n8n-1 \
  python3 -m pip show playwright
```

Expected version:

```text
Version: 1.48.0
```

Run a real Chromium test:

```bash
docker exec -i n8n-multi-n8n-1 python3 - <<'PY'
from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright

with sync_playwright() as p:
    browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=True)
    page = browser.new_page()
    page.set_content("<title>DigiExpress Playwright Test</title>")
    print("PLAYWRIGHT_OK")
    print("Chromium:", browser.version)
    print("Title:", page.title())
    browser.close()
PY
```

Verified production result:

```text
PLAYWRIGHT_OK
Chromium: 130.0.6723.31
Title: DigiExpress Playwright Test
```

### Using Playwright from n8n

For the current deployment, use an **Execute Command** node so the workflow runs against the Python/Playwright environment installed in the main n8n container.

Example command:

```bash
python3 - <<'PY'
from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright

with sync_playwright() as p:
    browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=True)
    page = browser.new_page()
    page.goto("https://example.com", wait_until="domcontentloaded")
    print("PLAYWRIGHT_OK")
    print("Title:", page.title())
    print("URL:", page.url)
    browser.close()
PY
```

### Zero-downtime production note

Playwright and Chromium were installed in-place on the running production container to avoid restarting or recreating n8n. Therefore, until the custom image is rebuilt and deployed during a maintenance window, do not recreate the running container solely for this change.

The repository now also includes a top-level `Dockerfile` containing the reproducible Playwright configuration for future image builds.
